    summary: "Model callbacks and notifications without retaining subscribers or losing asynchronous failures.",
    what: "A delegate is a type-safe callable reference. A lambda can create a delegate and capture variables from its enclosing scope. An event restricts how external code interacts with a notification, normally allowing subscription and unsubscription rather than arbitrary invocation.",
