    summary: "Use expressive data models without confusing init-only properties with deep copies.",
    what: "Records provide generated value-oriented behavior, while pattern matching expresses decisions from an object's shape and values. A with expression copies a record's state shallowly. Reference-valued members can therefore remain shared even when the record's own properties cannot be reassigned after initialization.",
