    summary: "Protect edits with concurrency tokens and make merge or retry decisions explicit.",
    what: "Optimistic concurrency compares the state originally read with the state being updated, commonly through a configured concurrency token. If the expected version no longer matches, the update can affect no row and EF can report a concurrency conflict. This differs from a transient connection failure.",
