    flow: "Representative cases -> versioned system -> independent measures -> human calibration -> regression decision -> monitoring",
    example: "Release comparison:\nA: fluent answer but unsupported policy claim -> grounding failure.\nB: correct refusal with no permitted evidence -> expected success.\nC: correct text but wrong account changed -> critical tool failure.\nDo not collapse these into a style-only score.",
    cheat: ["Separate retrieval quality from generated-answer quality.", "Keep held-out cases out of prompt tuning.", "Automated judges need calibration.", "Task correctness and action safety outweigh fluency."],
    pitfalls: ["Tuning repeatedly against the test set leaks the benchmark.", "Averages can hide a regression on permission-sensitive cases."],
    exercise: "Design a 20-case support evaluation with explicit evidence and outcomes. Choose critical release blockers, calibrate two disputed cases, and describe production drift monitoring.",
