    summary: "Update nested state without accidentally mutating earlier snapshots.",
    what: "Objects have reference identity. Object and array spread create shallow copies, so nested references can remain shared. Immutable updating means constructing changed paths deliberately; it is not achieved merely by writing const or spreading the top-level object.",
